  annotation = {中文辅助译名：通过多尺度卷积和协同特征增强的短时运动想象脑电图解码网络},
  abstract = {Motor imagery (MI) electroencephalography (EEG) has gained attention in brain–computer interfaces (BCIs) for stroke rehabilitation, assistive communication and numerous consumer electronics (CE) applications. However, reliable MI decoding typically relies on long observation windows, limiting responsiveness. To enable robust decoding from limited-duration EEG signals, this paper proposes ST-MSNet, a short-window MI-EEG decoding network that jointly addresses discriminative representation learning and optimization stability. ST-MSNet employs a multi-scale spatiotemporal convolutional architecture that couples spatial representation learning with independent temporal modeling at different receptive fields, enabling scale-specific rhythmic characterization while reducing feature competition across temporal scales. A lightweight feature synergistic enhancement module (FSEM) combines variance-based temporal statistical aggregation with adaptive temporal-channel feature refinement to retain informative responses while suppressing feature redundancy, thereby obtaining compact and discriminative representations from limited observations. In addition, a prediction entropy-driven robust curriculum learning strategy characterizes sample difficulty and progressively incorporates samples from easy to challenging, reducing the influence of highly uncertain samples during early optimization. ST-MSNet is evaluated on the BCI Competition IV 2a and High Gamma datasets across 1–4 s observation },
}

